# Run by the compositor once it is up, as the desktop's user.
#
# The task bar: without it a minimised window has nowhere to be found, which
# is the defect this whole environment exists to remove.
#
# The configuration is named, not left to be found. Left to itself the bar
# took its stock one - a start menu that wants an interpreter this image does
# not have, processor and memory gauges, and a clock, on a board with no
# battery-backed clock. Seen in the first screenshot of the trial.
sfwbar -f /etc/xdg/sfwbar/sfwbar.config &

# The session bus. The file manager decides whether it is the first of itself
# by claiming a name on it: with no bus the claim fails, it concludes that
# another one is already running, asks that one - which does not exist - to
# open a window, and exits. Nothing is drawn and nothing is reported.
dbus-daemon --session --address="$DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS" --nofork --nopidfile &
